"text": "How much could losing just one hour of sleep at night impact your body's ability to lose fat? It's more than you think. When you lose weight, it can come from one of two places: either from body fat or from lean body mass, like muscle. And sleep has more control over that than most people realize. But how much of a big difference could just one hour make? Researchers wanted to find out, so they took two groups of people and put them on the exact same calorie deficit. The only difference is that one group slept one hour less five nights per week, and the other slept uninterrupted. And after eight weeks of dieting, both groups ended up losing the same amount of weight on the scale, which isn't a surprise. But how much of that weight came from body fat? The group getting in normal sleep ended up losing about 83% of their weight from body fat and 17% from lean body mass. But the group who got just one hour less ended up losing 85% of their weight from lean mass and only 15% from body fat. But before you panic, keep in mind that these people weren't lifting weights, which is one of the best things you can do to protect your muscle while dieting. And your body can somewhat adapt to lower sleep over time, like in the case of new parents. But if everything else is dialed in, sleep might be one thing holding you back. Comment SLEEP if you want my free fat loss guide.",
